versions\n\nv4.4.1.stable.official [49a5bc7b6]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6607) - AMD Ryzen AI 9 HX 370 w/ Radeon 890M (24 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen right-clicking a `Resource`'s property that has `@export`, if that property is set to a `Script`, the inspector does not show the `Clear` button to set the property to `null`.\n\nThis is what I would expect to see:\n<img width=\"396\" height=\"498\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/248f99bb-8e42-4f23-ba0f-429718fc27ba\" />\n\nBut when the property is set to a `Script`:\n<img width=\"405\" height=\"537\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1c5df9b7-c95c-423a-8e51-8d2c25b2dfeb\" />\n\nAs you can see, the `Clear` button is not shown on the `Script`.\n\nThis happens regardless of the type of the property. Even when the property is typed to `Resource`, when setting it to a `Script` it still doesn't show `Clear`. Also, for some reason this issue does not apply when the property is exported from a `Node`.\n\nI'm guessing this is done to prevent people from clearing an object's script by clearing its `script` property, but this shouldn't apply to other properties.\n\nThis issue is preventing me from adding a custom revert value for `Script` properties, since they cannot (easily) be set to `null` again afterwards.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a custom `Resource` script.\n2. Add an `@export`-ed property of type `Script` (or an ancestor class).\n3. Create an instance of the custom `Resource`.\n4. Set the property to a `Script`.\n5. Right-click the property, and observe that the `Clear` button is missing.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22083437/mrp.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110178/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110178/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}